1. **Comparison of strategies**: My best overall strategy so far (Strategy 3) performed significantly better than the other two, with an average reward of 469.1/500 compared to 200.9/500 for Strategy 1 and 269.5/500 for Strategy 2.
2. **Importance of angular velocity**: I observed that when the pole angle is positive (i.e., the pole is leaning to the right) and the angular velocity is negative (i.e., the pole is rotating to the left), moving left with a probability of 0.7 helped to balance the pole more effectively. Similarly, when the pole angle is negative and the angular velocity is positive, moving right with a probability of 0.7 was beneficial.
